  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ヤナギバグミ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A4%E3%83%8A%E3%82%AE%E3%83%90%E3%82%B0%E3%83%9F",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106387078,
      "text": "ヤナギバグミ は、被子植物グミ科グミ属に属する植物で、中央アジアの乾燥地帯でよく見られる。沙漠などの乾燥に強く、タマリスクとコトカケヤナギと共に「沙漠の3英雄（植物）」とも呼ばれる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Elaeagnus angustifolia」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaeagnus_angustifolia",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1372332221,
      "text": "Elaeagnus angustifolia, commonly called Russian olive, silver berry, oleaster, or wild olive, is a species of Elaeagnus, native to Asia and limited areas of eastern Europe. It is widely established in North America as an introduced species."
    }
  },
